ESP32-S3: model I2C_ANA_MST.ANA_CONF0's BBPLL_CAL_DONE bit.

The esp32s3 machine has no model for the analog-master register block
(I2C_ANA_MST, 0x6000_E040), so it falls through to the catch-all
esp32s3.iomem region, whose read handler returns 0 for everything.

esp-hal's `clocks::request_pll_clk` -> `configure_bbpll` starts the BBPLL
self-calibration and then spins:

    while I2C_ANA_MST::regs().ana_conf0().read().bbpll_cal_done().bit_is_clear() {}

Bit 24 never sets in the emulator, so EVERY esp-hal guest hangs there --
inside `esp_hal::init`, before esp-println exists.  The symptom is an app
that the second-stage bootloader loads and verifies and that then prints
literally nothing (the bootloader is ESP-IDF C and never touches this
register, which is why the boot log looks perfect right up to
"Loaded app from partition").

Model just enough to be correct from the guest's point of view: remember
what the guest wrote to ANA_CONF0 and OR in BBPLL_CAL_DONE on read, i.e.
"the calibration you just started has already converged".  The two
stop_force bits stay writable/readable so the guest's read-modify-writes
behave; nothing else about the block is claimed.

Harness-side per CLAUDE.md's QEMU isolation rule -- the guest image is
byte-identical to what ships.

--- a/hw/xtensa/esp32s3.c
+++ b/hw/xtensa/esp32s3.c
@@ -458,8 +458,23 @@
 }
 
 
+/*
+ * I2C_ANA_MST (analog master) — only ANA_CONF0 is modelled, and of it only
+ * enough that a guest which starts a BBPLL self-calibration sees it finish.
+ * Offsets are relative to ESP32S3_IO_START_ADDR.
+ */
+#define ESP32S3_I2C_ANA_MST_ANA_CONF0   0xe040
+#define ESP32S3_BBPLL_CAL_DONE          (1u << 24)
+
+static uint32_t esp32s3_ana_conf0;
+
 static uint64_t esp32s3_io_read(void *opaque, hwaddr addr, unsigned int size)
 {
+    if (addr == ESP32S3_I2C_ANA_MST_ANA_CONF0) {
+        /* BBPLL calibration is instantaneous here: the guest's
+         * `while (!bbpll_cal_done) {}` would otherwise never terminate. */
+        return esp32s3_ana_conf0 | ESP32S3_BBPLL_CAL_DONE;
+    }
 #if ESP32S3_IO_WARNING
     warn_report("[ESP32-S3] Unsupported read to $%08lx, size = %i\n", ESP32S3_IO_START_ADDR + addr, size);
 #endif
@@ -469,6 +484,10 @@
 
 static void esp32s3_io_write(void *opaque, hwaddr addr, uint64_t value, unsigned int size)
 {
+    if (addr == ESP32S3_I2C_ANA_MST_ANA_CONF0) {
+        esp32s3_ana_conf0 = (uint32_t) value & ~ESP32S3_BBPLL_CAL_DONE;
+        return;
+    }
 #if ESP32S3_IO_WARNING
         warn_report("[ESP32-S3] Unsupported write $%08lx = %08lx\n", ESP32S3_IO_START_ADDR + addr, value);
 #endif
